-- 5. Seed Privacy Policy v1 em inglês
INSERT INTO public.legal_documents (doc_type, version, locale, content) VALUES (
  'privacy',
  1,
  'en',
  E'# Privacy Policy\n\n_Last updated: publication date._\n\n> **Notice:** This text is an initial template and should be reviewed by a legal professional before production use, especially for GDPR/LGPD compliance.\n\n## 1. Data Controller\n\nNEVVOH is the controller of personal data collected through the platform, in accordance with applicable data protection laws.\n\n## 2. Data Collected\n\n**Data provided by the User:**\n- Name, email, password (stored as a hash).\n- Tax data (for paying customers): tax ID, legal name, address.\n- Generated content: tasks, comments, attachments, ideas, meeting minutes.\n\n**Data collected automatically:**\n- IP address, browser type, operating system.\n- Platform access and usage logs.\n- Essential cookies for authentication.\n\n## 3. Purpose of Processing\n\nWe use your data to:\n- Deliver the contracted Service.\n- Authenticate and secure your account.\n- Issue invoices and process billing.\n- Send operational and commercial notifications (the latter with consent).\n- Comply with legal obligations.\n\n## 4. Legal Basis\n\n- **Contract performance**: for most platform features.\n- **Consent**: for marketing communications.\n- **Legal obligation**: for retention of tax data.\n- **Legitimate interest**: for security and fraud prevention.\n\n## 5. Sharing\n\nWe do not sell personal data. We share only with:\n- Infrastructure providers (hosting, transactional email) under confidentiality agreements.\n- Authorities, when required by law.\n\n## 6. Storage and Security\n\n- Data is stored on cloud servers with encryption in transit (HTTPS) and at rest.\n- We apply role-based access control (RLS) and tenant isolation between customers.\n- Daily automatic backups.\n\n## 7. Retention\n\n- Account data: while the account is active.\n- Tax data: for the period required by tax legislation (minimum 5 years).\n- Audit logs: up to 24 months.\n- After cancellation, data may be anonymized or deleted upon request, respecting legal obligations.\n\n## 8. Data Subject Rights\n\nAt any time, you may:\n- Confirm the existence of processing of your data.\n- Access, correct, or request deletion of your data.\n- Withdraw consents.\n- Request portability.\n- File a complaint with the relevant data protection authority.\n\nTo exercise your rights, contact us via support or the email below.\n\n## 9. Cookies\n\nWe only use essential cookies for the operation of the platform (authentication). We do not use third-party tracking cookies without explicit consent.\n\n## 10. Data Protection Officer (DPO)\n\nFor data protection matters, contact us via the platform support channel.\n\n## 11. Changes to this Policy\n\nWe may update this Policy periodically. Material changes will be communicated by email or on the platform.\n\n---\n\nLast review: initial version.'
);